KONOHAGAKURE — BINGO BOOK UPDATE PROCEDURE

The Bingo Book is the village's register of high-priority targets — missing-nin, enemy shinobi, and threats — with threat ratings and, where authorized, bounties.

Procedure:
- Nominations for entry originate from intelligence reports, mission debriefs, or the T&I Force and are reviewed by the Hokage's office.
- Each entry records name, last-known affiliation, abilities, threat rank, and engagement guidance (capture vs. flee-on-sight).
- Threat ratings are revised as new field intelligence arrives; deceased targets are annotated and archived.
- Distribution is restricted to appropriate ranks; the book is not civilian-releasable.
- Cross-village threat entries (e.g., Akatsuki members) are coordinated with allied intelligence where an alliance exists.

Entries are maintained alongside the S-rank missing-nin ledger. See the Bingo Book folder for current threat files.
Maintained by the village intelligence division.
